@cindex package-local nicknames
@defgena{add-local-nickname,@middlepackage{}} client package @
  local-nickname nicknamed-package

TODO: mention extension?
TODO: return value

Change the @termrefl{package-local nickname,package-local nicknames}
within @var{package} such that @var{local-nickname} refers to
@var{nicknamed-package} @emph{in the package system specified by
@var{client}}.

@var{package} is a package object to which the pair of
@var{local-nickname} and @var{nicknamed-package} is to be added.
@var{local-nickname} is a string that represents the local nickname to
be used to refer to @var{nicknamed-package}.  @var{nicknamed-package} is
the package object to be nicknamed.

If the pair of @var{local-nickname} and @var{nicknamed-package} exists
in @var{package} already, then the call to this function has no effect.
If a pair of @var{local-nickname} and a different nicknamed package
exists in @var{package} already, then an error of type
@classref{nickname-refers-to-different-package-error,@toppackage{}} is
signaled.

This function can be used to implement and customize the
@emph{semi-standard} function
@funref{add-package-local-nickname,@toppackage{}}.

The default method, if necessary, adds the pair of @var{local-nickname}
and @var{nicknamed-package} to @var{package} using the accessor
@genref{local-nicknames,@lowpackage{}} and adds @var{package} to
@var{nicknamed-package} using the accessor
@genref{locally-nicknamed-by,@lowpackage{}}.
@end deffn

@cindex package-local nicknames
@defgena{remove-local-nickname,@middlepackage{}} client package @
  local-nickname

TODO: mention extension

Remove the @termref{package-local nickname} @var{local-nickname} from
@var{package} and return @emph{true} if @var{package} has been changed
and @t{nil} otherwise.

@var{local-nickname} is a string that represents the local nickname to
be removed from @var{package}.  @var{package} is a package object from
which @var{local-nickname} is to be removed.

If @var{local-nickname} is the @termref{package-local nickname} of any
package in @var{package}, then it is removed, and this function returns
@emph{true}.  If @var{local-nickname} is not the @termref{package-local
nickname} of any package in @var{package}, then this function has no
effect, and returns @var{nil}.

This function can be used to implement and customize the
@emph{semi-standard} function
@funref{remove-package-local-nickname,@toppackage{}}.

The default method, if necessary the local nicknames of @var{package}
contain a pair of @var{local-nickname} and a nicknamed package
@var{nicknamed-package}, removes the pair from @var{package} using the
accessor using the accessor @genref{local-nicknames,@lowpackage{}} and
removes @var{package} from @var{nicknamed-package} using the accessor
@genref{locally-nicknamed-by,@lowpackage{}}
@end deffn

@node Middle Package-symbol Relation Functions
@section Middle Package-symbol Relation Functions

@defgena{find-symbol,@middlepackage{}} client package name

Try to find a symbol named @var{name} in @var{package} and return two
values: The first value is either a symbol with the name @var{name} that
is accessible in @var{package}, or @code{nil} if there is no such
symbol.  The second value is either @code{:internal}, @code{:external},
@code{:inherited}, or @code{nil}.

@middleimplements{f,find-symbol}

@cindex export status
The default method on this generic function calls
@code{(@genref{symbol-entry,@lowpackage{}} @var{client} @var{package} @var{name})}
to potentially obtain a present symbol and the export status of the
symbol.  If such a present symbol exists, the associated export status
determines whether the second return value is @code{:internal} or
@code{:external}.  If there is no such present symbol, the method makes
similar calls to @genref{symbol-entry,@lowpackage{}} for packages on the
use-list of @var{package}.  If one such call yields a symbol with export
status @code{:external}, the method returns that symbol and
@code{:inherited}.  If no accessible symbol is found, the method returns
@code{nil nil}.
@end deffn

