@node Middle Environment Functions
@section Middle Environment Functions

@defgena{packages,@middlepackage{}} client

Return a list of all package objects in the package system designated by
@var{client}.

@middleimplements{f,list-all-packages}

The default method on this generic function simply calls
@t{(@genref{packages,@lowpackage{}} @var{client})} and, if necessary,
copies the returned list since the standard requires the return value to
be a freshly allocated list.
@end deffn

@defgena{find-package-using-package,@middlepackage{}} client package name

Find, in relation to @var{package}, and return the package named
@var{name} in the package system designated by @var{client} or return
@code{nil} if no such package exists.

The default method on this generic function behaves like
@speclink{f,find-package}.

For the @ref{Package-local Nicknames} extension, a method specialized to
@classref{local-nicknames-mixin,@middlepackage{}} extends the behavior
of this generic function such that it first looks for @var{name} in the
@termrefl{package-local nickname,local nicknames} defined in
@var{package} and returns the nicknamed package, if any, before
executing the default behavior.
@end deffn

